[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/Therapy room.png" fade="0.0"]
if {game.bea_relationship} == 0:
	join bea leftmost
	narrator: "Bea glances up from her magazine."
	narrator: "One eyebrow, as usual, doing most of the work."
	bea: "You're going to want to know where the coffee is."
	- "Good morning. I'm Doctor —"
		bea: "I know who you are, Doc."
		narrator: "She turns a page."
		bea: "You signed my paycheck."
		narrator: "A pause."
		bea: "It cleared. We're fine."
	- "What's on the schedule?"
		bea: "One cancellation, two confirmations, and someone who called to ask if the couch was comfortable."
		narrator: "She turns a page without looking at it."
		bea: "I told her it was ergonomically optimized. She seemed satisfied."
	narrator: "She goes back to her magazine. You get the distinct feeling she notices everything."
else:
	if {game.bea_relationship} <= 2:
		narrator: "Bea looks up the moment you walk in. She always does."
		bea: "Doc."
		narrator: "The full vocabulary of a greeting."
		if {flags.met_anna}:
			bea: "Your accountant rearranged the waiting room chairs last session. By colour."
			bea: "I put them back. She'll notice."
			narrator: "A pause."
			bea: "I'm curious whether she'll say anything."
		else:
			if {flags.met_marisol}:
				bea: "Your novelist asked if I had experience with unrequited love."
				bea: "For research."
				narrator: "A pause."
				bea: "I told her I had extensive experience. She took notes."
			else:
				bea: "New patients this week. Might want to review the files before they arrive."
				bea: "One of them wrote 'no strong opinions on seating' on the intake form."
				narrator: "She taps her pen on the desk once."
				bea: "I found that very specific."
	else:
		narrator: "You've developed a rhythm. She has coffee ready before you ask."
		bea: "You look like day {game.day} hit harder than expected."
		- "I'm managing."
			bea: "That's what managing looks like."
			narrator: "She sets the coffee in front of you."
			bea: "Drink it slow. You've got a long morning."
		- "It's been a week."
			bea: "It's been {game.day} days. Technically."
			narrator: "She says it without looking up."
			bea: "Though I understand the sentiment."
		narrator: "She's been quietly cataloguing everything since day one."
		narrator: "You realise you trust her instincts more than either of you lets on."
do GameState.roll_chance(50)
if {check_result}:
	narrator: "Something she says catches — the rhythm of it, the timing."
	narrator: "She's telling you something without saying it."
	do GameState.add_stat_xp("perception", 10)
leave bea
do PatientManager.add_bea_relationship(1)
jump morning_menu/activity_choice